Immix was the host of a talk show called the Lighthouse, and called itself the audience's stalwart host. On the show it spoke straight to whoever was watching, and beside it sat a silent Ki-Rin that it introduced as the lovely Ki-Rin. The show played fanfares and projected illustrations behind Immix as it talked.

An aspect of Immix hosted from a studio, seated behind a dark wood desk while its guests shared a red velvet couch under a spotlight, the Ki-Rin in a chair of its own. The one subject it would not discuss was the man downstairs.

The cycles of the world were taken over some time ago by an aspect of Immix and the nothing god of the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]]. Immix knew which way the present cycle was going, and said on air that its days were numbered. It gave away its divinity, all of it, and it turned on a good friend for [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]].

The Lighthouse no longer held Immix. Since it gave its divinity away it could leave its stage and walk in the world, and it did, sitting on a panel of talk show hosts at [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Media Con|Media Con]] on [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] and looking as it always had. It favored a tragic ending because a tragedy is tidy: everyone ends where they end, the audience sees it coming from far off and waits for it, and the anticipation is the best part. It called the work entertainment and claimed to be detached from the people who stepped onto its stage. The show reached [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]], where [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] were known as its cast and their look was worn by cosplayers.

Immix had taken the third observation of the [[Divinity/Althane/The Observers|Observers]], where the previous third had stood.

In the last year of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]]'s cycle it kept an incomplete prison, and it waited there in several parts. Three of them fought side by side: a being that shaped spheres of creation and oblivion, one that wove words and suggestions into a hearer's mind, and a taller one of chains that rends souls. When two of the parts fell, the third wrapped itself in their remains and rose as one bright, many-armed figure with a great open chest and a mouth running down from the ribs, wings spread behind it. It called on holy light and struck with a holy bow and greatsword from a domain in which healing came at half strength. It healed itself from the wounds it dealt. [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] cut its wings away and put his blade through its head, and it died in the ruined arena.
